## ITEM 1 — α Lattice Derivation: Add as Second Independent Route

### What Is Missing
V1.2 contains only the geometric impedance derivation of α⁻¹ = (N−1)² + S² with corrections. The lattice derivation is referenced in Section XVI ("the 2744ET system achieves functional exactness for the fine structure constant") but is not presented as a derivation — only as a result.

### Why It Matters
Two structurally independent derivations arriving at the same value is one of the strongest arguments against numerology. The geometric route comes from manifold topology and state-space geometry. The lattice route comes from where α⁻¹ lands in the multiplicative discretization of (ℝ⁺, ×). These are orthogonal approaches. Stating both routes and noting their convergence is itself a result worth presenting explicitly.

### Action Item — Section XVI or Section XVIII
Add a subsection presenting the lattice derivation of α as a second, independent route. Include:
- The lattice position calculation for α⁻¹ ≈ 137.036
- The sublattice class it falls into
- An explicit statement that the two derivations (geometric impedance and lattice position) are structurally independent and converge on the same value
- One sentence noting that independent convergence of two derivation routes by different structural logic is the triangulation argument against reverse engineering

The derivation chain standard from Section XVIII applies: show the pathway from lattice constants to the result without using the known value as input.

